Here's a slightly updated version of the #sit patch. It now combines the
following patches:

   #sitting at a pit gives an appropriate message. (Due to Joshua Kwan.)
   #sitting on a box makes it shatter if you're heavy.
   #sitting on a cream pie goes "Yecch!" and destroys the pie. (New!)

The differences from the first time I posted this patch, in
<Pine.LNX.4.60-041.0511171508420.16716@unix41.andrew.cmu.edu>...

   Fixed an apparent typo ("life.." for "life.") in Joshua Kwan's
     pit-sitting patch.
   Sitting on a box won't "tear to shreds" scrolls or spellbooks in it.
   The cream pie "Yecch!".

Enjoy!

   Now I think I'll try the "throwing water on scrolls" YANI. I'm thinking
that thrown potions of water should blank scrolls and rust armor, but not
dilute other potions (they're in closed containers!) or spellbooks 
(they're also normally closed, and besides, that would be too evil).

-Arthur,
patch follows


